SUMMARY:Deadline: MIT Museum: BRAIN Digital Content Open Call
DESCRIPTION:The MIT Museum seeks proposals for compelling digital content e
 xploring humanity's relationship with the BRAIN\, the museum's thematic fo
 cus from April to September 2027 bringing together art\, science\, technol
 ogy and design on cognition\, neurotechnology\, brain-computer interfaces\
 , mental health and the boundaries of ability. Selected proposals run as a
 mbient content on the two-story digital screen (3840x3024\, 80:63 aspect r
 atio\, 20'3" x 16'2") in the museum's central Exchange amphitheater. The m
 useum wants immersive\, non-linear\, experimental\, non-didactic work\, su
 ch as artful visualizations of data or scientific phenomena\; interactivit
 y (touchscreens\, QR codes) is out of scope and content-critical audio is 
 discouraged. Content must run on the museum's existing hardware (Windows P
 C with RTX 3090\, NEC LED wall with Analog Way 4K system). WHO CAN APPLY: 
 artists\, scientists\, engineers\, designers and other creative practition
 ers\, from MIT or the broader community. SUPPORT: flat honorarium of USD 2
 \,500-5\,000 per selected proposal\; no additional development funding. Ap
 plications reviewed from 2 November\, accepted list finalized January 2027
 . Deadline: 1 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: MIT Museum\nLocation: Cambri
 dge\, Massachusetts\, US (content shown on-site\; remote creation possible
 )\nAward: Flat honorarium of USD 2\,500 to 5\,000 per selected proposal\, 
 at the Museum's discretion\nDuration: BRAIN thematic focus runs April - Se
 ptember 2027\; selection finalized January 2027\n\nMore: https://mitmuseum
 .mit.edu/brain-digital-content-open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mitmuseum.mit.edu/brain-digital-content-open-call?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US (content shown on-site\; remote cre
 ation possible)
